From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:13:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] recore: keep U-Boot's console output off the panel

Recore drives a printer's front panel over HDMI. With vidconsole in
stdout, every line U-Boot prints during a normal boot is drawn on it
before the boot script shows its splash image. Keep stdout on serial
only. stderr keeps vidconsole, so errors still reach the panel.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
 include/configs/sunxi-common.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
index 49d5617f..9cd97f1d 100644
--- a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
+++ b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
@@ -254,7 +254,7 @@
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_VIDEO
 #define CONSOLE_STDOUT_SETTINGS \
-	"stdout=serial,vidconsole\0" \
+	"stdout=serial\0" \
 	"stderr=serial,vidconsole\0"
 #else
 #define CONSOLE_STDOUT_SETTINGS \
-- 
2.47.3

